      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey can u give me a quick checklist for wcag 2.1 compliance for a mobile app? specifically looking for the main things we need to hit for color contrast and making sure it works with screen readers. thx",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For WCAG 2.1 compliance, here's a checklist for color contrast and screen reader compatibility in a mobile app:\n\nColor Contrast:\n- Ensure 4.5:1 color contrast ratio between text and background (Href color scheme, Color Definition, and text Inverted).\n- Test for web content's 3:1 color contrast ratio requirement.\n\nScreen Reader Compatibility:\n- Provide semantic HTML5 tags for header, footer, and main content.\n- Implement ARIA attributes for interactive elements (links, buttons, and images).\n- Ensure text remains readable when zoomed out or on a smaller screen.\n- Use aria labels for custom and non-standard elements (e.g. custom buttons).\n\nNote: These are the main considerations, but it's recommended to conduct a thorough accessibility audit and test your app with various devices and screen readers for a comprehensive assessment.",
